    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicators per approved project document on 20 March 2020:
1.1 Level of capacity of the Government (separately national and sub-national) demonstrated on the following areas: 
&apos;inclusiveness&apos; and &apos;responsiveness&apos; (Perception: proportion of participants in the civic engagement mechanisms who believe decision making is inclusive and responsive)
1.3 Level of sustainability of CSOs
1.4 Level the authorities&#x2019; attitude (verbal and behavioral) assessed by CSOs members interviewed (Likert scale: 5 points)
2.1 Number of engagement infrastructure supported (disaggregated by):  National and Sub-national
2.2  Level of effectiveness of the existing infrastructure by users 
(disaggregated by): Sex, Age, Geographical locations (% of perception by users of the infrastructure if it is improved) 
2.3 % of participation of the following populations in the infrastructure: Women&#x2019;s groups, Youth&#x2019;s groups, and Other marginalized groups
3.1 % of civil servants think of CSOs as equal partners 
3.2 # of ideas that are co-designed and jointly implemented by the government and civil society

Revised indicators as per revised project documents on 14 Oct 2022:
1.1 Percentage of participants applied the following capacities after learning sessions: 1- Citizen and stakeholder engagement, 2- problem solving, 3- Data literacy and evidence, 4- Enabling creative environment, 5- System thinking, 6- Storytelling and advocacy.
1.2 Level of confidence in the following capacities learned: - Citizen and stakeholder engagement, 2- problem-solving, 3- Data literacy and evidence, 4- Enabling creative environment, 5- System thinking, 6- Storytelling and advocacy.
1.3 # of prototypes supported to support CSOs sustainability
2.1 # of engagement infrastructure supported with the government and CSOs capacity development (disaggregated by): National and sub-national.
3.1 % of participants in co-design who thinks CSO-Government relationship improved
3.2 # of ideas that are co-designed and jointly implemented by the</narrative>
    </description>
